    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1127">

                <pb facs="1315" n="1119" xml:id="pg1119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.85/7–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1127<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clayton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1127-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-21">July 21, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi>–185.
                    From Clayton.</p>
                <p>Admiral Land, Mr. Dunn, and I have discussed Polish seamen’s
                        strike<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1127-f2"/> (reurtels Nos. 73 and 74<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1127-f3"/>) and
                    decided that WSA should take action parallel to
                    British; that is, haul down Polish flag, run up United States flag, offer to
                    sign on same seamen, and indicate that the action is temporary for the emergency
                    situation.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
